+# Research
+
+## Causes
+
+- `ProductCommonFacadeImpl.deleteProduct(Long, MerchantStore)` loads the product for the merchant and calls `ProductService.delete`, which removes the product. There is no preservation step for carts or orders.
+- `ShoppingCartServiceImpl.getPopulatedShoppingCart` resolves every persisted cart item by SKU in `getPopulatedItem`. A deleted product returns `null`, marks the item obsolete, and causes `getById`/`getByCode` to mark the whole cart obsolete and delete it. This is why a cart containing one deleted product cannot be opened, and why a cart containing only that product disappears instead of becoming an empty cart.
+- `ReadableShoppingCartMapper` assumes every cart line has a non-null live `Product` (`readableMinimalProductMapper.merge(item.getProduct(), ...)`) and calculates display totals from the cart's remaining line items. Deleted lines therefore must be removed before mapping/calculation. An empty line-item set naturally produces zero totals and quantity.
+- `ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.createCartItem` already calls `productService.getBySku` and throws `ResourceNotFoundException` when the product is absent, so adding a deleted product is intended to be a 404. The multi-item path (`createCartItems`) also rejects a missing SKU, but its current size check is fragile and needs to preserve the same 404 behavior.
+- Checkout builds order products from hydrated cart items. `OrderProductPopulator` currently resolves the product live and fails if it is absent; after deletion, checkout must only see surviving cart lines, so deleted lines must be removed during cart hydration before checkout.
+- `OrderProduct` stores the purchased SKU, name, quantity, one-time charge, prices, attributes and persisted order totals. `ReadableOrderProductMapper` and the deprecated `ReadableOrderProductPopulator` use those stored values for the response and only enrich the optional nested live product when a current product is found. That optional enrichment must remain non-fatal so merchant and customer order reads continue after deletion.
+
+## Affected files and paths
+
+- Cart lifecycle and cleanup: `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java`.
+- Cart API conversion and add/multi-add behavior: `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java` and `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/cart/ReadableShoppingCartMapper.java`.
+- Order snapshot response mapping: `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/order/ReadableOrderProductMapper.java` and `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/order/ReadableOrderProductPopulator.java`; order facade paths use these for private and authenticated single/list reads.
+- Product deletion: `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/product/ProductCommonFacadeImpl.java`, exposed by `ProductApi` and `ProductApiV2`.
+- Deleted SKU lookup: `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/product/ProductFacadeV2Impl.java` and `ProductApiV2` (`GET /api/v2/product/{sku}`); the facade already throws `ResourceNotFoundException` when lookup returns null.
+
+## Other effects to protect
+
+- Do not change product deletion semantics or any other product's lookup.
+- Do not recalculate or derive order prices from a live product: order responses must continue using persisted order-product values and persisted order totals.
+- Cart cleanup must delete orphaned cart attributes and persist the surviving line-item set, but must not delete the cart or mark it obsolete merely because all product lines were removed.
+- Checkout, cart PUT and multi-add must operate on the cleaned cart; a deleted SKU must never reach order creation or payment.
